<title>RUSSIA: LOMO expects 1996 pre-tax profit of 7 bln rbls.</title>
<headline>LOMO expects 1996 pre-tax profit of 7 bln rbls.</headline>
<dateline>ST PETERSBURG, Russia 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian optical goods manufacturer LOMO said on Monday it expects a pre-tax profit of seven billion roubles for 1996 after a profit of 21.7 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>OAO Leningradskoye Optiko-Mekhanicheskoye Obyedineniye (LOMO) posted a profit for 1996 despite losses in the first three quarters after carrying out some export orders in the last three months, said Lazar Zalmanov, head of public relations.</p>
<p>Sales rose to about 230-240 billion roubles from 146 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
